& [Implementation] is one effect-free PowerShell orchestration layer over ordinary build tools
  + resolves one revision to exact commit tree and timestamp identities
  + resolves revisions through verify and end-of-options so caller text cannot become a Git option
  + creates one Git archive and extracts it into two distinct source roots
  + measures rustc and Cargo from both extracted roots and refuses divergent toolchain selection
  + builds into two initially absent target roots with locked offline Cargo fixed source epoch disabled incremental state and MSVC reproducible linking
  + compares executable length SHA-256 and bytes by bounded streaming
  + invokes only contract field-digest and verify against each executable
  + requires exact verifier-computed report identity and exchange count in addition to terminal latch and assurance disposition
  + emits one stable JSON receipt without random temporary paths

& [Safety] constrains local temporary state
  + the campaign root must be a direct child of repository target with an exact generated-name grammar
  + default operation removes the campaign root after success or failure
  + diagnostic retention is explicit and declares retention without disclosing its random path in the receipt
  + inherited build environment variables are restored in a finally block

& [ProofShape] separates execution evidence from a static repository audit
  + the build tool is the fresh expensive proof route
  + the audit binds preserved source canonical signature implementation controls receipt identity tested Git object current tracked build-input freshness retained report identities and all three tested-to-receipt-to-anchor Git histories without rebuilding
  + two successive default campaigns against toolchain-and-verifier-hardened implementation commit 43b2f51 emitted the same receipt
  + an earlier retained-artifact campaign against the cleanup-hardened predecessor produced the same source tool artifact and behavior identities with only the declared retention boolean changed
  + the pinned receipt is an ordinary successor record over its tested commit and makes no impossible self-inclusion claim

& [SupportDelta] is local reproducibility made executable and inspectable
  + FADL_F009 now has a proven controlled local successor profile
  + historical h8 remains unchanged and retains only deployment content identity

& [RequirementDelta] remains outside this solution
  + cross-machine and cross-toolchain reproducibility
